    "page": "case_23.html",
    "image_path": "assets/work.jpg",
    "alt": "Two people working together at a laptop, with one person pointing at its screen.",
    "image_html": "<img alt=\"Two people working together at a laptop, with one person pointing at its screen.\" class=\"photo\" id=\"target\" src=\"../assets/work.jpg\"/>",
    "context_html": "<article class=\"article\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">The work issue / People &amp; practice</p><h1 class=\"display\">Better work starts<br/>with a conversation.</h1><p class=\"intro\">What two people and a shared screen can teach us about finding a way forward.</p><p class=\"byline\">By the Common Ground editorial team · 6 minute read</p><img alt=\"Two people working together at a laptop, with one person pointing at its screen.\" class=\"photo\" id=\"target\" src=\"../assets/work.jpg\"/><p class=\"caption\">A collaborative working session.</p><section class=\"section\" id=\"details\"><p>There is a moment in a good conversation when a difficult problem starts to feel possible. Someone points to a detail. Someone else asks a question. The shape of the work changes.</p><h2>Make the thinking visible.</h2><p>Shared notes, simple sketches, and a screen everyone can see give a team something concrete to discuss. The next step becomes easier to agree on.</p></section><blockquote><h2>Leave enough space for a different point of view.</h2></blockquote></article>",
    "control_type": null,
    "control_text": "",
    "control_aria_label": null
  },
